# File Dialog Example

This is a simple C++ program that demonstrates how to open a file dialog to select a file path.

## Prerequisites

- A C++ compiler (e.g., GCC, Clang, MSVC)
- C++17 or later

## Usage

1. Compile the program using your C++ compiler:
   ```sh
   g++ -std=c++17 main.cpp -o file_dialog_example
   ```

2. Run the compiled program:
   ```sh
   ./file_dialog_example
   ```

3. The program will open a file dialog where you can select a file.

## Code Explanation

### `main.cpp`

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <fstream>
#include <string>

int main() {
    std::string filePath;

    // Open a file dialog to select a file
    std::cout << "Please select a file:" << std::endl;
    std::cin >> filePath;

    // Check if the file exists
    std::ifstream file(filePath);
    if (!file) {
        std::cerr << "Error: Unable to open file." << std::endl;
        return 1;
    }

    // Read and process the file
    std::string line;
    while (std::getline(file, line)) {
        std::cout << line << std::endl;
    }

    file.close();
    return 0;
}
```

